// Shown when Signe dies (her last wound). The game then goes back to her last
// rest at home, framed as a memory she had wrong: in a game where memory is
// power, even her death is something she misremembers.
// DRAFT by Claude, for Daniel to rewrite.

=== death ===
{~The ice closes over you, and the cold is very quiet.|The last wound opens, and for a moment the snow is warm.|Black water, then nothing at all.}
No.
{~That isn't how it went. You're remembering it wrong.|That isn't what happened. You must be remembering it wrong.|You've misremembered. It didn't end like this.}
{~Go back to what you are sure of: {name_known():Signe, } by the fire, at home.|Think back. The last thing you are sure of is resting at home.|Start from what you know. You were home. You were warm.}
-> END
